#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Every function's description and grants, in one place. Regenerates
# functions/<name>/<name>.json; never edit those by hand (bin/fnjson.py, as Tasks').
#   table   read        table:rw  + write rows        table:rwd  + delete rows
#   function:<name>     run it        workflow:<name>     start and read its runs
#   connector:<id>      use it        /folder:verbs       a folder
# No function can be granted schedule.create, a table's public rows, a web
# widget, contact outreach or another plugin's parts, so those are done by the
# app as the person (README, "What only a person can do").
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
f() { uv run --no-project python bin/fnjson.py "$@"; }
FILE="triage_settings triage_report:rw triage_item:rw triage_event:rw triage_rule triage_correction ask:rw away connector:github connector:slack workflow:triage-read function:triage_needs_you"
f triage_report_add "File a bug, alert, security problem or request (title, body, quote: the person's words, source_url: a link to their message, via: chat, slack, teams or email; reporter_name, handle_kind and handle when it was someone else). Reads it, matches it to what's open, counts reach, suggests an owner, and answers with the item's number and what's known ('Filed as T-48; 1,240 people hit the same thing'). A question is not filed." $FILE
f triage_lookup "What's known about some words (text): the open and recently fixed items that match, each with its number, state, reach and owner, and what the team published as known. Use before filing, or when someone asks whether something is broken." triage_item triage_report triage_known
f triage_on_report "A report was written (the triage-report-added trigger): read, match, ask, reach, owner, mark down, tell. Leaves a report already filed alone." $FILE
f triage_on_form "A visitor's answer to the report form (the triage-form-added trigger, with row_author): made a report from the contact the platform names, the email typed, or an unnamed visitor, with its page, version, browser and screenshot, and filed." $FILE triage_form:rw
f triage_on_github "A GitHub webhook on a watched repository: issues (opened, reopened, closed; issue forms read field by field), issue_comment (+1 adds an asker), dependabot_alert, code_scanning_alert, secret_scanning_alert (opened files a report; fixed or dismissed closes the item)." $FILE
f triage_on_slack "A new message in a watched Slack channel (lemma-platform#1245's channel trigger): a report is filed; a question or chatter is left alone and counted." $FILE
f triage_poll "Every 15 minutes: Sentry and PostHog issues with people and events, the watched Slack channels until their trigger is live, and GitHub issues and security alerts since the last read; updates reach on what's open, wakes snoozed items, and keeps each source's state in words." $FILE triage_settings:rw connector:sentry connector:posthog
f triage_reach "Work an item's reach out again (item: id, number or T-48; empty for every open item): people, events, who asked, companies, a 24-hour trend, escalating, and the priority that follows." triage_settings triage_report triage_item:rw ask
f triage_read "Ask triage_reader for the Lemma's read of one item (item): what it is, what each source answered, what couldn't be checked, the files, a fix hint. Runs on its own from 25 people and for high security alerts." triage_settings triage_item:rw triage_report workflow:triage-read
f triage_read_save "Keep triage_reader's read on its item: summary, evidence (every source not checked named, with why), paths, fix hint." triage_settings triage_item:rw triage_event:rw
f triage_decide "A person's decision on an item (item; action: accept, agent, decline with reason, duplicate of, refuse_duplicate, snooze until or days, mark_down with reason, bring_back, split report_id, owner user_id and name, record). Accept makes a team task with the evidence; decline tells the askers why; duplicate moves them onto the original. Never call it for the team unless a person decided." triage_settings triage_report:rw triage_item:rw triage_event:rw triage_rule triage_correction:rw triage_known:rw ask:rw away task:rw connector:github connector:slack workflow:triage-read function:triage_needs_you
f triage_on_task "A Triage task's status changed (the triage-task-changed trigger): done makes the item done, tells the askers where they asked (or leaves them for Release notes), resolves Sentry issues and closes the GitHub issue if chosen; canceled puts it back in the inbox." triage_settings task triage_report triage_item:rw triage_event:rw triage_known:rw ask:rw connector:github connector:slack connector:sentry function:triage_needs_you
f triage_tell "Tell the people who asked about an item (item, text), each where they asked: a GitHub comment or a Slack thread reply, once per place. dry_run says who would be told and sends nothing." triage_settings triage_item ask:rw triage_event:rw connector:github connector:slack
f triage_publish_known "Publish an item as a known issue in the team's words (item, title, state: investigating, being_fixed or fixed, page: an address prefix), for the report form and the visitor chat." triage_item triage_known:rw triage_event:rw
f triage_unpublish_known "Take an item off the known issues list (item)." triage_item triage_known:rwd triage_event:rw
f triage_join_known "For the visitor chat beside the report form, opened to contacts: add the visitor (contact_id, set by the platform) to a known issue (known_id), so they hear when it's fixed." triage_known triage_item ask:rw triage_event:rw
f triage_needs_you "What in Triage needs the person, in the shared needs_you list (Today reads it): decide an urgent item when they're on triage this week, and tell people who used the form. Runs as the person; resolves what no longer applies." triage_settings triage_item ask away needs_you:rw
f triage_setup_save "Keep Triage's set-up (only the fields given): repositories, rotation, Slack channels, Sentry, PostHog, the report form, acknowledgements, thresholds; done writes the memory block. Safe to run again." triage_settings:rw function:triage_memory
f triage_away "Someone away (member_id, name, start, end, part full or half), one row per day in the shared away table; clear takes the days out. Who's on triage skips them." away:rwd
f triage_memory "Tells this Lemma's agents that Triage is installed: its own block in /memory/AGENTS.md and its guide at /memory/plugins/triage.md, leaving the team's notes alone. Set-up runs it; safe to run again. remove takes both out." /memory:read,write
f triage_sample_data "load: a sample morning to look around (a checkout crash reported four ways, a billing spike, two security alerts, Slack reports that look like an older item, a GitHub issue, two marked down; made-up people at .example addresses, nothing posted outside). clear: removes only what the sample made." triage_settings:rw triage_item:rwd triage_report:rwd triage_event:rwd triage_correction:rwd ask:rwd triage_known:rwd triage_rule:rwd task:rwd triage_sample_row:rwd function:triage_needs_you
